# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — never commit it.
# Read by scripts/factory-secrets.sh. See DESIGN.md's "GH_PAT: token
# strategy" and docs/adr/0001-design-to-issues-loop.md for the full picture.

# From `claude setup-token` (Claude Code OAuth, not an API key — see
# README.md's Setup section for why: this authenticates against your Claude
# subscription, not pay-per-token billing). Copied verbatim into every new
# project's own CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN secret. Safe to reuse across every
# project: it's a Claude subscription credential, not a GitHub one, so a
# leak costs quota, not repo access.
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# GH_PAT deliberately does NOT live here, and factory-secrets.sh will not
# read one from this file even if you add it.
#
# CORRECTED 2026-08-17 — this file originally held a single reusable
# "All repositories" GH_PAT, on the reasoning that minting one is more
# convenient than one per project. That reasoning is exactly backwards for
# blast radius: the same value gets copied into every generated project's
# own GH_PAT secret, so a leak from ANY ONE of them exposes a token that can
# act on ALL of them, plus every future one — precisely the shared-credential
# problem ai-app-factory's own GH_PAT was narrowed to avoid, just relocated
# rather than removed.
#
# factory-secrets.sh now prompts for GH_PAT interactively (input hidden)
# every run instead: mint a fresh fine-grained PAT scoped to "Only select
# repositories: <that one repo>" (it must already exist — run factory-new.sh
# first) with Contents, Issues, Pull requests, Actions, Secrets (Read and
# write), paste it at the prompt, and it's never written to disk. More
# friction per project; a leak from one project can never reach another.
